# Proposed (milestone2.md, "BallVector", "Values": the constructor): the finish of bv_make_k. It is
# norm_finish_1 under a mask that also says the radius is not negative: a negative radius, as a NaN
# one, makes the result the whole space. norm_finish_1 alone, the finish of the other ball vectors,
# whose radii are nonnegative by construction, does not test the sign; so the constructor needs a
# finish of its own, whose claim (finite_or_nan under the mask ok and the sign of the value) the
# vocabulary has not: one more field, `nonneg`, of finite_or_nan, would say it.
kernel:        bv_make_finish
input:         rz
input:         mask ok
output:        r
output:        mask flag
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   the outputs are those of norm_finish_1, after a test of the sign

p         = le(0, rz)
q         = and(ok, p)
(r, flag) = norm_finish_1(rz, q)
